{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_342","type":"agent_message","text":"Temp probe cleanup was blocked by policy; it lives outside the workspace at `D:\\tmp\\s04probe` and does not affect the repo.\n\n**What I did**\n\nThis is a verification/ledger packet (S04 / TF-0279) whose scope is a fixed 5-file deliverable set — no product code change. It pins which `agent_browser` actions actually reach which existing gate, and records the residual set instead of over-claiming.\n\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s04-browser-effect-boundary.md` — two-gate ledger (connection-mode gate vs session-ownership gate) + per-action coverage matrix + explicit residuals.\n- `tests/unit/browser-effect-boundary-ledger.test.ts` — pins the real policy functions (deny/allow matrix over external/derived-untrusted/missing/invalid vs trusted system / direct operator) and statically asserts action coverage (`click`/`type` gated; `evaluate`/`command`/`close` residual).\n- `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-browser-effect-boundary.md` — task spec (validates clean).\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/s04-acceptance.json` — acceptance evidence.\n- `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/S04-SHA256SUMS` — manifest for the four files.\n\n**Key findings (verified against real code)**\n\n- Connection-mode gate: external/unknown provenance is denied for `auto-connect`/`cdp`/`external-profile`, allowed for `managed`; trusted/operator unrestricted.\n- Session-ownership gate: `click`/`type` only; requires Main-reported `connection.mode === 'managed'` for external/unknown.\n- Residual (not claimed covered): `evaluate`, `command`, `close`, and reuse of pre-existing external sessions by non-click/type actions.\n- No weakening: SSRF/private-network config, browser kill-switch flags, and Main's `allowExternalBrowser` acknowledgement unchanged. Single existing policy reused.\n- Only the 5 target files were created; nothing else in the tree changed.\n\n**Honest caveat:** this isolated workspace has no `node_modules` and 